#X text 1672 449 SET RELAY (added 2026-08-21) -- buffer_manager.pd now also forwards a "set <fullstem> <ringarrayname>" message (see its own SET RELAY comment) once a ring-buffer compose finishes\\\, so this instance actually plays the freshly-composed segment instead of always replaying the full \$1-mono buffer from position 0 Route (obj 1) gained a 5th "set" case -> a new per-stem "route vocals melody bass drums" (mirroring the prepare dispatch at obj 2) -> each stem's remainder (just the array name\\\, e.g. "ring_1_bss") gets re-tagged with a genuine "set" selector (list prepend alone doesn't produce one\\\, same fix as everywhere else) and sent into that stem's slot_router_stem instance -- same inlet0 prep/commit/stop/resume already share\\\, since stem_timestretch~.pd's own route now has a matching "set" case (added 2026-08-21) that just needs the message to arrive with its normal selector., f 70;
